%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:socket-override -- the open command of a socket selects another algorithm.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the open command of a socket can choose another one".

The classes: the nine algorithms of the package inet.transportlayer.tcp.flavours (TcpNewReno is
the default, TcpReno the value of LegacyTcp, TcpCubic of LinuxTcp), qualified-alias (a
qualified NED type name), unknown (a name without a NED type: an error) and socket-override
(the open command of a socket selects another algorithm). Each test of an algorithm checks a
behavior that none of the other eight algorithms shows. The code:
TcpConnection::createTcpAlgorithm() and the classes of the algorithms. The test passes with each value of the parameter by design, so the cross-class check skips
it.

Host under test: host1, with the parameter TcpNewReno, whose application selects TcpTahoe on
its socket before the open. Observation: level 3, the algorithm of the connection of host1 is
inet::tcp::TcpTahoe when its SYN goes.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: socket-override
%# value: "TcpNewReno"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassSocketOverride")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setTCPAlgorithmClass("TcpTahoe");
            app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000);
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "tcpAlgorithm.className == \"inet::tcp::TcpTahoe\"")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassSocketOverride compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpNewReno"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassSocketOverride: PASS
